    "created_at": "2026-10-01T18:23:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-01T18:23:59Z",
    "body": "This still appears current in Chromium.\n\n`USBDevice` caches `configuration_index_`; `EnsureDeviceConfigured()`, `FindInterfaceIndex()`, endpoint availability, etc. all operate from that cached state. I don't see a platform re-query before configuration-dependent operations.\n\nA useful regression test would be: externally change configuration, then call an operation whose validity differs between the old and new configurations. That would make the desired stale-state behavior concrete before changing the implementation.\n",
